\description{
Reads one USDA NASS Quick Stats bulk dump from disk and returns the
requested series as source-native admin-statistics rows: one row per
reporting unit, item, indicator and year, with values converted to WHEP
units and every non-numeric NASS value code preserved.

The dump is streamed a chunk of lines at a time and filtered chunk by
chunk, so the ~8 GB flat file is never materialised. Only the fifteen
columns this reader uses are parsed, and a gzipped dump is read without
being extracted first.

Identifiers stay exactly as NASS published them: no item is mapped to a
WHEP \code{item_prod_code} and no unit is resolved to a polity. Both happen
downstream, from the source-native keys returned here.
}
\section{Series selection}{

NASS keys a series on \code{SHORT_DESC}, which folds the commodity, its class,
the production practice and the statistic into one string
(\code{"CORN, GRAIN - ACRES HARVESTED"}). \code{short_desc} is therefore the item
selector, and its default covers the field crops and livestock species
the subnational spatialization needs. The authoritative item-to-series
table is built separately; pass \code{short_desc} to read anything else.

Rows are kept only where \code{SOURCE_DESC} is \code{"SURVEY"} (not the
quinquennial census), \code{DOMAIN_DESC} is \code{"TOTAL"} (not a breakdown by
farm size, sales or NAICS class), and \code{PRODN_PRACTICE_DESC} is
\code{"ALL PRODUCTION PRACTICES"} (not the irrigated or organic split).
}

\section{Reference periods}{

Crop area is annual (\code{FREQ_DESC == "ANNUAL"}) and its final estimate
carries \code{REFERENCE_PERIOD_DESC == "YEAR"}; the in-season forecasts
(\code{"YEAR - AUG FORECAST"} and siblings) are excluded by that default.
Livestock inventories are \code{FREQ_DESC == "POINT IN TIME"} and the default
reference period is \code{"FIRST OF JAN"}.

One species does not follow that default: NASS publishes the annual hog
inventory as of \strong{1 December}, so \code{"HOGS - INVENTORY"} has no
\code{"FIRST OF JAN"} rows at all and returns nothing under the default. That
is deliberately not patched here -- which hog reference period stands for
the annual inventory is a vocabulary decision, not a reading one -- but
it is never silent: any requested \code{short_desc} that matches no row warns
by name, and \code{reference_period} selects a different one.
}

